div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Marshall, J. May switch\nto affirm</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>City of Milwaukee et al. v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/08145274-8e91-4df9-a84f-57f982a886ca.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1678/1182\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J. Delaware can&#x27;t rely on\n[underlined: Wyandotte]. State law\nhas no place here at all.\nwas federal common\nlaw displaced by stat\nlaw? I say yes</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>City of Milwaukee et al. v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/60a762cc-2564-419d-b68f-120616961124.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1676/2191\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J. Illinois can&#x27;t rely on\nWyandotte. State law\nhas no place here at all.\nWas federal common\nlaw displaced by stat\nlaw? I say yes</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>City of Milwaukee et al. v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/2167f706-d961-4118-8a6c-baaf7545a562.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1925/2486\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>White, J. Prior opinion made\nfederal law controlling\nlaw &amp; only question\nis preemption by stat.\n1) overflows 2) can\nfederal court set\nhigher standards\nthan EPA. EPA\ndoesn&#x27;t address overflows\nbut where it really\nhas set a standard\nthere&#x27;s preemption. But\nI affirm the holding was\nbased on preemption, but\nfailure to prove a nuisance\n\nMa\nto</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>City of Milwaukee et al. v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/2175e186-6c92-4f3a-a9d6-7cb05916fe31.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1554/1937\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Blackmun, J. BRW speaks for\nme agreeing with\n7^th Circ reversal\n— there is some\npreemption here\nas [underlined: to] treatment\nstandards</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>City of Milwaukee et al. v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/4633bafb-dfcb-4431-8b0d-d37d11c4f02a.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1823/2182\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Powell, J. [underlined: Preemption] to\nextent of treatment\nstandards.\nAm concerned\nabout proof of injury or\nthreat of injury - finding\nis only &quot;maybe&quot; these\nhorrors [underlined: could] happen,\nnot that they had\nhappened. So would\nreverse for failure of\nproof. So only, a prepon-\nderance enough or is\nclear &amp; convincing required</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>City of Milwaukee et al. v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/627437c8-f0a3-460e-afc1-60d3ce43fd80.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1620/2250\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Rehnquist, J. There is preemption\nby 1977 Act to extent\nit covers subject\nmatter of law-suit.\nEPA standards\nsupersede common\nlaw of nuisance [struck: to]\nagree with BRW as\nto extent of occupancy\nof field. On storm\nsewers, do permits\nprescribe standards —\nif so maybe go all\nway with WJB</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>City of Milwaukee et al. v. Illinois et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/99562672-c7b1-44f9-a246-d2f9b6191a08.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1843/2342\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stevens, J. Agree with BRW\nthat judgment should be\naffirmed\nEvidence does prove\nactual injury in Illi-\nnois\nThought original\ngrant was only on\nlimited preemption issue\nBut grant was across\nthe board\nThink a tough venue\nquestion here — Ill probably\nwrong but don&#x27;t want\nto reverse on that\nIs it &quot;preemption&quot; to\nsay statute not common\nlaw governs</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>Scindia Steam Navigation Co., Ltd. v. De Los Santos et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/4410df69-4683-4cfe-8182-b2b4a561b79c.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1539/1955\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Blackmun, J. statute offers\nlittle guide but the\nlegis history does</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>Scindia Steam Navigation Co., Ltd. v. De Los Santos et al.</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/309445f0-02ef-420d-b33f-4de349c0db94.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1380/1858\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Rehnquist, J. agree with\nLFP + Friendly</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>United States v. Difrancesco</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/aef4a841-2f5b-4fde-af73-c20c51a511a4.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1624/1384\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Marshall, J. Thinks Govt\ncant get 2 bites at\ncherry.</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>United States v. Difrancesco</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/478ecfc5-ecc3-4a49-bffb-d8ad2127d9e2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1753/1287\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Stewart, J. Only ques is\npres whether statute\nviolates double Jeop.\nClause - I don&#x27;t think\nit does [struck: but] because\nI&#x27;d reject Benz dictum</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>United States v. Difrancesco</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/5f087598-f5bd-4af7-9411-12c5acb99da2.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1679/2140\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>White, J. Put aside\ndangerous offender\nquestion. Getting to\ndouble Jeopardy issue\ndon&#x27;t think definition of\nfinal provides answer.\nHave to determine whether\nDJ clause objectives are\nviolated by this statute\nNot sure I&#x27;m at\nrest but now I&#x27;d\naffirm</pre></div></div></article></div></div>","<div class=\"head\"><div><p class=\"kicker\">1980 term</p><h2>United States v. Difrancesco</h2></div><div class=\"pager\"><span class=\"count\"></span><button data-step=\"-1\" aria-label=\"Previous\">&#8249;</button><button data-step=\"1\" aria-label=\"Next\">&#8250;</button></div></div>\n<div class=\"spread\"><div class=\"sheet\"><img src=\"https://panoptes-uploads.zooniverse.org/subject_location/f73681c6-ec01-41c5-b1b8-040c042b0ee1.jpeg\" class=\"z\" alt=\"The full page\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1549/1857\" decoding=\"async\"></div>\n<div class=\"boxes\"><article class=\"box\"><div class=\"pair single\"><div class=\"r r1\"><h4>Whole page</h4><pre>Blackmun, J. An affirmance\nhere would put in\nshadow whole con-\ncept 7 appellate review\n7 sentences. Dont\nsee merit in DSO issue\nan DJ issue will\nreverse for now</pre></div></div></article></div></div>"]